      "pageDescription": "Northwest Ohio Loses Another Media Outlet. News from Williams, Fulton, and Defiance counties in The Village Reporter. Local coverage from Northwest Ohio.",
      "evidenceText": "Northwest Ohio Loses Another Media Outlet | Sports Close Menu Home Subscribe Current Edition Store Locations Photo Albums Rate Card Classifieds Contact Us Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Saturday, November 14 Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram YouTube TikTok Login News Northwest Ohio Loses Another Media Outlet By Newspaper Staff October 4, 2023 Updated: October 4, 2023 No Comments 2 Mins Read Share Facebook Twitter Email Copy Link It is with a heavy heart that we announce the cessation of operations for TiffinOhio.net, effective Friday, October 6, 2023. This decision has not been made lightly, and we want to take a moment to explain the reasons behind it. Since our inception in 2016, TiffinOhio.net has been committed to delivering comprehensive and up-to-date local news coverage for our beloved community. Over the years, we have been honored to be your trusted source for news, events, sports, politics, entertainment, and more. However, like many other media outlets, we have faced significant challenges in recent years, particularly stemming from the COVID-19 pandemic that struck in early 2020. The pandemic led to decreased advertising revenue, making it increasingly difficult for us to sustain the high-quality journalism and services you have come to expect from TiffinOhio.net. As we move forward, Dylan J. Poe, our founder, and the dedicated team that has contributed to the efforts of Tiffin Publishing LLC will be embarking on new ventures and opportunities. We want to express our deepest gratitude to each and every one of you—our loyal readers, subscribers, and the entire Tiffin and Seneca County community—for your unwavering support throughout the years. It has been an incredible journey, and we are proud to have been a part of this vibrant community. While TiffinOhio.net will no longer be a part of your daily news routine, we hope that the spirit of community engagement and local journalism will continue to thrive in Tiffin and Seneca County. We encourage you to seek out other reputable sources of news and information to stay informed about the issues that matter most to you. Once again, thank you for your trust, support, and readership. It has been an honor to serve this community, and we will cherish the memories and connections we’ve made along the way. If you have any questions or would like to get in touch, please feel free to reach out to us through our contact information on our website until our closure on October 6, 2023. With heartfelt gratitude and warm regards, Dylan J. Poe Editor, TiffinOhio.net Director, Tiffin Publishing LLC Help us keep covering our neighbors. A tip goes 100% to newsroom coverage. Or pick another way to support local news: Leave A Newsroom Tip Subscribe Buy A Physical Copy Advertise With Us Having a garage sale? Place a classified ad &rsaquo; Previous Article DELTA VILLAGE COUNCIL: Financial Housekeeping Tops Council Meeting Next Article BRYAN BOARD OF PUBLIC AFFAIRS: Bryan BPA Announces 2023 People’s Choice Tank Of The Year Award Details Related Posts Four County Ambassadors From Archbold, Wauseon, Fairview & Evergreen Speak To Rotary November 14, 2026 News Delta Administrator Suggests Comprehensive Zoning Review As Nova Plan Advances November 14, 2026 News Two Teens Hurt In Four-Vehicle Crash On County Road AC In Clinton Township November 14, 2026 News Northwest Ohio Home Prices Rise As Housing Market Enters Seasonal Slowdown November 13, 2026 News Comments are closed. Subscription Account Login Local Sponsor New Feature Who Made Local News This Week? Select an edition to view names BROWSE EDITIONS Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Manage Consent To provide the best experiences, we use technologies like cookies to store and/or access device information. Consenting to these technologies will allow us to process data such as browsing behavior or unique IDs on this site. Not consenting or withdrawing consent, may adversely affect certain featu