      "pageDescription": "ESPN NFL analyst Rex Ryan faces multiple charges after allegedly running over the feet of pedestrians and then leaving the scene.",
      "evidenceText": "Rex Ryan arrested after allegedly hitting pedestrians with truck Skip to content Credit: Kirby Lee-USA TODAY Sports By Matt Yoder on 11/11/2026 11/15/2026 Less AI and more AA in your search results. ESPN NFL analyst Rex Ryan is facing four charges after being arrested following an incident in Nashville. According to The Tennesseean , Ryan was driving his pickup truck downtown when he allegedly ran over the feet of two pedestrians who were attempting to cross Broadway while the former coach was making a right turn. Of course, anyone in the know will find that to be incredibly ironic given Ryan’s well-documented love of that particular body part. Rex Ryan then drove away from the scene and was chased down by the pedestrians. According to the reports, Ryan then left his vehicle at a stop light to engage in an argument with them before driving away once again. Afterwards, the people who were hit took a photograph of the truck and its license plate and called police. It was later then traced back to Ryan, and he turned himself in to the authorities on Wednesday morning. Naturally, TMZ has already published a photo of his mug shot. The 63-year-old is now facing multiple charges stemming from the incident, including leaving the scene of an accident, failing to give information or render aid, and failing to obey a traffic signal. His bond was set at $6,000. When reached by Awful Announcing for comment about the situation, ESPN issued a statement that said, “We are aware and are in touch with Rex.” Ryan was head coach of the New York Jets and Buffalo Bills during his time in the NFL after winning a Super Bowl as defensive coordinator of the Baltimore Ravens. He has been an ESPN analyst since 2017 as one of the network’s top analysts, appearing on a number of shows including Sunday NFL Countdown and Get Up. Rex Ryan is a self-proclaimed “ toe expert ,” so if anyone should have checked on someone’s feet after being run over by a truck, then it should have been him. About Matt Yoder Matt writes the Awful Announcing 'The A Block' newsletter every Wednesday. Subscribe here . View all posts by Matt Yoder Follow on Twitter Related Content The WNBA has figured out the best way to handle manufactured outrage: ignore it The 76ers are either building a superteam or creating a superproblem Is a sports media blue wave coming, too? Why Joe Buck and Troy Aikman is the most painful breakup in sports media history Recent Posts Rose’s first regular show since his ESPN layoff premieres in January. \"This is the type of stuff the Chiefs are studying this week.\" \"I just deal with so many young players now, and I’m just like, 'You’re how old?'\" \"Jacobs, their fine running back, is back.\" \"It is against the law to leave your feet. No jumping.\" The series declined by 2% versus last year. Sidebar Popular Posts The top five candidates to replace Ernie Johnson on ‘Inside the NBA’ The Dave Portnoy ‘Big Noon Kickoff’ breakup was always inevitable How to fix the ManningCast Five NFL teams play three consecutive primetime games this season; zero did so last year. Mike Florio thinks he knows why Five players who deserved to win the Heisman Trophy but didn’t The SEC’s TV ratings dominance is getting scary for the Big Ten Recent Posts Rose’s first regular show since his ESPN layoff premieres in January. \"This is the type of stuff the Chiefs are studying this week.\" \"I just deal with so many young players now, and I’m just like, 'You’re how old?'\" \"Jacobs, their fine running back, is back.\" \"It is against the law to leave your feet. No jumping.\" The series declined by 2% versus last year.",
