      "pageDescription": "“Face the Nation” boss Mary Hager is leaving CBS News, Status has learned. But she’s not the only major figure at the Sunday program saying goodbye.",
      "evidenceText": "Facing the Exits Facing the Exits “Face the Nation” boss Mary Hager is leaving CBS News, Status has learned. But she’s not the only major figure at the Sunday program saying goodbye. Oliver Darcy Nov 11, 2026 Facing the Exits “Face the Nation” boss Mary Hager is leaving CBS News, Status has learned. But she’s not the only major figure at the Sunday program saying goodbye. Oliver Darcy Nov 11, 2026 On Wednesday, \"Face the Nation\" boss Mary Hager had some important news to disclose to her colleagues: After more than three decades at CBS News , where she has not only led the venerable Sunday public affairs program, but also served as executive editor of politics since 2022, her time at the network was coming to an end. As Hager explained to staffers, she had made the difficult decision to leave CBS News. Hager's departure represents a significant loss for CBS News. While her official title is senior executive producer of \"Face the Nation,\" she played an outsized role in CBS News' Washington bureau. A 35-year veteran of the network, she possesses a wealth of institutional knowledge, having helped steer its political journalism through multiple presidential elections and various political cycles. But Hager, who I’m told had informed network leadership of her intent to exit her role over the summer, isn't the only major figure at \"Face the Nation\" departing the show. Status has learned that … The rest of this story is for paid subscribers only. Unlock the Rest Already a subscriber? Sign in . Scoop-driven reporting and sharp-edged analysis. See why The Wall Street Journal declared Status a “must-read.” Keep reading VIEW MORE About Us Archive Go Premium Quick Links Home Power Lines Archive Shop Gift About Us Advertise With Us Authors Oliver Darcy Jon Passantino Natalie Korach Brian Lowry Status is the definitive nightly briefing that cuts through the noise to inform readers about what is really happening in the corridors of media power. JOIN © 2